 ('In which surah are the verses of the first revelation found?', 'Al-‘Alaq', ['Al-Fatiha', 'Al-Baqara', 'Al-Kawthar'], 'The first verses beginning with “Iqra” are at the start of Surat al-‘Alaq.', 'First revealed surah'),
 ('Which angel conveys God’s revelation to the prophets?', 'Gabriel (Jibril)', ['Michael', 'Israfil', 'Azrael'], 'The angel of revelation is Gabriel; he conveyed the Quran to Muhammad.', 'Angel of revelation'),
 ('The month in which the Quran began to be revealed is Ramadan.', 'Al-Baqara 185 states that Ramadan is the month in which the Quran was sent down.', 'The Quran and Ramadan'),
 ('By what name does the Quran call the night on which its revelation began?', 'The Night of Power (Laylat al-Qadr)', ['The Night of Forgiveness', 'The Night of Desires', 'The Night of Ascension'], 'Surat al-Qadr says the Quran was sent down on the Night of Power.', 'Night of Power'),
 ('Who was the first to believe in the Prophet?', 'Khadija', ['Umar', 'Uthman', 'Hamza'], 'According to many sources the first believer was Khadija, followed by Abu Bakr, Ali and Zayd (TDV).', 'First believer'),
 ('Between which cities was the Hijra?', 'From Mecca to Medina', ['From Medina to Mecca', 'From Mecca to Ta’if', 'From Jerusalem to Mecca'], 'The Prophet and the Muslims migrated from Mecca to Medina because of persecution.', 'The Hijra'),
