 ('According to a hadith, “religion is sincerity (nasiha)”.', 'The hadith in Muslim stresses that the essence of religion is sincerity and sincere counsel.', 'Religion is sincerity'),
 ('In a hadith, to what are the believers likened in relation to one another?', 'A building whose parts support one another', ['Separate islands', 'Leaves blown by the wind', 'Racing horses'], 'The hadith says a believer is to a believer like a building whose parts support each other (Bukhari, Muslim).', 'Unity of believers'),
 ('What was Medina called before the Hijra?', 'Yathrib', ['Ta’if', 'Khaybar', 'Badr'], 'Medina’s earlier name was Yathrib; after the Prophet’s migration it became “the City of the Prophet”.', 'Old name of Medina'),
 ('Who was the first caliph after the Prophet?', 'Abu Bakr', ['Umar', 'Uthman', 'Ali'], 'After the Prophet’s death, Abu Bakr became the first caliph.', 'First caliph'),
